        "original_id": "5edd15c3-fa77-5bc3-9261-41a1870f2abb",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Frank Augustus Miller\n- Places: Riverside, California, United States\n- Organizations: Frank Augustus Miller Middle School\n- Products: The Mission Inn Hotel & Spa\n- Concepts: Mission Revival Style, architectural styles\n\nFacts:\n- Frank Augustus Miller was born on June 30, 1858.\n- Frank Augustus Miller was the owner and chief developer of the Mission Inn in Riverside, California, United States.\n- Frank Augustus Miller Middle School in Riverside was named after Frank Augustus Miller.\n- The Mission Inn in downtown Riverside, California, is now known as The Mission Inn Hotel & Spa.\n- The Mission Inn Hotel & Spa is a historic landmark hotel.\n- The Mission Inn Hotel & Spa is a composite of many architectural styles.\n- The Mission Inn Hotel & Spa is generally considered the largest Mission Revival Style building in the United States.\n- Frank Augustus Miller died on June 17, 1935.",
